# Windows "mark of the web" alternate-data-stream marker files. These get
# created automatically by Windows Explorer whenever you extract a .zip that
# was downloaded from the internet -- one per extracted file, named
# "<filename>:Zone.Identifier". They're inert (Neovim/git never read them,
# wrong extension for anything to load) but they clutter every directory
# listing and diff. Safe to delete; this keeps them out of the repo.
*Zone.Identifier

# Standard Neovim/editor noise
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
